CIS I — Assignment 1: Pivot Calibration¶
This notebook walks through the pivot-calibration scenario from the assignment (Figure 1): a pointer and a calibration object, each carrying a marker body, observed by an optical tracker. Your job is to design the marker-sphere layouts and workspace placements, then calibrate the pointer's tip position p_tip to within about 2mm.

Everything runs against src.simulation, a self-contained simulator that plays the role of the physical tracker + hand-guided robot + calibration sensor described in the handout. It injects measurement noise — your code never sees ground truth except where explicitly noted for validation/reporting in Step 8 (real hardware wouldn't give you that; the point there is to report your achieved accuracy, not to use the ground truth in your calibration math itself).


